    {
      "origin": "pitchingwrx/pitchingwrx-reports",
      "sha": "ba329c9590d2176dbde2ade6f29323f1987b9e78",
      "message": "Fix count-column corruption and enable CSV uploads\n\n- _fix_count() (pwrx_db.py) and fix_count() (generate_report.py) used the\n  wrong reversal formula for count values Excel auto-converted to dates,\n  silently misattributing real counts to the wrong bucket instead of\n  recovering them (e.g. a real \"1-2\" was being written back as \"0-1\").\n  Root-caused and fixed via a real paired CSV/XLSX export of the same 80\n  pitches: Excel parses \"B-S\" as Month-Year when S==0 (bare \"0\" reads as a\n  2-digit year) and as Month-Day of the current year otherwise. Corrected\n  formula (balls=month, strikes=0 if year==2000 else day) verified with\n  zero mismatches across all 80 real pitches.\n- CSV uploads have never actually worked: pd.read_excel() cannot parse CSV\n  bytes at all, but every endpoint hardcoded the temp file as .xlsx\n  regardless of the real uploaded format. This is very likely why the count\n  corruption happens in the first place -- a failed CSV upload gets worked\n  around by resaving as .xlsx in Excel, which is exactly the action that\n  corrupts the count column. Fixed main.py to preserve the real uploaded\n  extension, and made pwrx_db.py/generate_report.py's file readers\n  extension-aware (.csv -> pd.read_csv, else -> pd.read_excel).",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pitchingwrx/pitchingwrx-reports/commits/ba329c9590d2176dbde2ade6f29323f1987b9e78",
      "request": {
