      "origin": "anjapope/digitalcollection",
      "sha": "f4667a22e34047c0bb6450b75da233eb902cfd96",
      "message": "fix(editorial-workbook): replace IFNA with IFERROR in Placement lookup formulas\n\nIFNA(VLOOKUP(...)) was producing #NAME? errors for all automatic\nPlacement columns (Room ID, Room name, Location, Supported type,\nCapacity) in the target Excel environment. Replace it with IFERROR,\nwhich is universally supported and behaves identically here since the\nwrapped VLOOKUP only ever fails with #N/A.\n\n- utilities/editorial-workbook/build.mjs: swap IFNA -> IFERROR in all\n  5 automatic lookup formulas, preserving lookup ranges and fallback\n  text ('Unknown slot' / 'Unknown room').\n- Regenerate ArchIvory Editorial Workbook.xlsx with the corrected\n  formulas; automatic columns now populate correctly (verified via\n  build.mjs inspect output and workbook.py check).\n- Add a regression test asserting build.mjs never reintroduces IFNA\n  in the generated formulas.\n\nValidation: all 30 editorial-workbook tests pass, workbook.py check\nreports unchanged counts (27 Placements / 45 Slots / etc.), all 12\nroom-placement tests pass, and the Jekyll build succeeds. No slot IDs,\nanchors, room geometry, or _data files were touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>",
