    {
      "origin": "AstermarkLabs/End-Shift",
      "sha": "11092a9409323b49237572e4b03b063dc70154a3",
      "message": "Task #30: Prevent importing a completely empty spreadsheet after all bad rows are skipped\n\nWhen every task row in a spreadsheet contains a formula error (e.g. #REF!,\n#VALUE!), the parser skipped all rows and returned an empty \"General Tasks\"\nsection with skippedRows > 0. The client's generic \"No tasks were found\"\nmessage didn't explain why.\n\nChanges in artifacts/api-server/src/routes/spreadsheet-import.ts:\n\n1. parseSpreadsheet now tracks formulaErrorRows separately from the existing\n   skippedRows counter. Formula-error rows (task/section cell matches\n   EXCEL_ERRORS) increment both; blank-task rows increment only skippedRows.\n   The return type now includes formulaErrorRows.\n\n2. The route handler checks taskCount === 0 && result.formulaErrorRows > 0\n   and returns HTTP 422 with the message:\n   \"All rows contained formula errors \u2014 check the spreadsheet for #REF!,\n   #VALUE!, or other error cells. No tasks were imported.\"\n\n3. The targeted 422 fires only when formula errors caused the empty result,\n   not when the file is simply all-blank rows (which the client handles with\n   its existing \"No tasks were found\" message).\n\n4. The log call includes formulaErrorRows alongside skippedRows for\n   observability on successful imports.\n\nDeviation from original spec: split skippedRows into two counters to avoid\nsurfacing a misleading formula-error message on all-blank-row files (code\nreview comment addressed).\n\nNo client-side changes required; the existing catch block in\nimport-checklist.tsx already surfaces server error messages verbatim.\nTypecheck passes cleanly.\n\nReplit-Task-Id: 3932df30-7039-442f-af18-806337199980",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/AstermarkLabs/End-Shift/commits/11092a9409323b49237572e4b03b063dc70154a3",
      "request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/AstermarkLabs/End-Shift/commits/11092a9409323b49237572e4b03b063dc70154a3",
