    {
      "origin": "syedhamzaali2k25-alt/Google-Sheets",
      "sha": "90fe33aab76c21164eb1c6bed13edcd0aed60b7d",
      "message": "Add spreadsheet health scoring engine and endpoint\n\n- backend/analysis/health_score.py: compute_health_report() scores a\n  spreadsheet 0-100 across five categories (data quality, formula\n  quality, structure, maintainability, security), each scored 0-100 by\n  deducting per-severity penalties from findings, then combined into an\n  overall score via configurable CategoryWeights (20% each by default,\n  normalized if they don't sum to 1)\n- checks per category: duplicate rows, blank required-looking fields,\n  invalid email/phone formats, inconsistent column types (data\n  quality); formula errors (#REF!/#DIV/0!/etc.), inconsistent formulas\n  across a column, broken references (formula quality); empty columns,\n  merged cells, hidden sheets, irregular table shapes (structure);\n  complex/nested formulas, unclear or missing headers, hard-coded\n  values mixed into formula columns (maintainability); emails, phone\n  numbers, SSNs, AWS keys, and generic secret patterns (security)\n- each finding carries category, severity, a human-readable\n  description, the affected cell range, and a recommendation; the\n  report's findings list is sorted highest-severity first\n- new endpoint POST /sheets/{spreadsheet_id}/health, accepting an\n  optional `weights` override and reusing the existing 401/403/404\n  error handling (plus 400 for weights that sum to zero)\n- takes both the SpreadsheetStructure (Step 2) and the raw Sheets API\n  response (Step 1) as input, since several checks \u2014 duplicates,\n  blanks, formula error values, PII-looking cell content \u2014 need actual\n  cell values that the normalized structure intentionally omits\n- renamed structure.py's column_letters/cell_ref/cell_is_non_empty\n  helpers from private to shared so health_score.py can reuse them\n- extended the Step 2 fixture with a formula error, a column with no\n  header, and a fake email address (it already had a duplicate row and\n  an empty column from Step 2), and updated Step 2's tests for the\n  fixture's new dimensions\n- backend/tests/test_health_score.py covers at least one failing case\n  per category plus scoring math, severity sorting, custom/zero\n  weights, and a clean-spreadsheet baseline (22 tests total, all\n  passing)\n\nCaught and fixed a real bug while writing tests: duplicate-row\ndetection hashed each row's raw cell values directly, which crashed\nwith TypeError on any row containing a formula-error cell (value is an\nunhashable dict) \u2014 exactly the kind of row this tool needs to handle.",
